<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Nafin Rate for March falls to 24.08 pct.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Nafin Rate for March falls to 24.08 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican state development Bank Nacional Financiera announced on Friday that its so-called Nafin Rate for March would be 24.08 percent, down 342 basis points from the previous month.</p>
<p>It said it was the third consecutive drop in the rate, which has fallen 10.7 percentage points since December. The Nafin Rate is that charged by the bank on its loans to small and medium-sized firms.</p>
<p>((--Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
</text>
